  <constraints>
    <constraint type="architecture">Compilation is enhancement, not gate. A story with status 'done' can have compilationStatus 'failed'. These are orthogonal fields. The compilationStatus field must never block story completion.</constraint>
    <constraint type="types">All type additions to functions/shared/types/epic-workflow.ts MUST be mirrored in src/types/epic-workflow.ts. Both files define the EpicStory interface — one for backend, one for frontend.</constraint>
    <constraint type="events">Compilation events use the existing futurator-agent-events table and pushEvent() mechanism. Events have a 7-day TTL (expireAt). Events must include jobId, stepId, agentId for correlation with the pipeline event stream.</constraint>
    <constraint type="error-handling">The try/catch for the COMPILE phase must be at the right level — wrapping all three compile steps. Individual step failures within the COMPILE phase should be captured, but the outer pipeline should continue to mark the story as completed.</constraint>
    <constraint type="log-fallback">When the COMPILER agent fails, the daemon itself must write the failure record to knowledge/log.md. This requires the daemon to have write access to the project workspace (it already does via workingDir).</constraint>
    <constraint type="backward-compat">Existing stories without compilation should have compilationStatus undefined (not 'skipped'). The field is optional in the type definition. Only stories processed after this feature is deployed will have a compilationStatus value.</constraint>
  </constraints>

